# Copy this file to deploy/.env and fill in the host-specific values.
# deploy/.env is gitignored and never committed.
#
# This is the SINGLE source of truth for both the host supervisor and the
# Docker stack (compose api + web). Editing this file on a fresh machine
# is all that is required to deploy the factory there.
#
# Both halves of the stack load this file:
#   - supervisor : `deploy/start_supervisor.sh` sources it before uvicorn.
#   - docker     : `docker-compose.yml` references it via env_file.

# ── Runtime / project roots ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are HOST-SIDE paths. They are read by the supervisor and the daemon
# when they run on the host. The Docker API container itself overrides
# AI_DEV_FACTORY_RUNTIME_ROOT to /runtime (the volume mount inside the
# container) — see docker-compose.yml.
#
# Adjust the path to match where you cloned the runtime tree, e.g.
#   ~/runtime/ai-dev-factory          (default)
#   /srv/ai-dev-factory               (production-style layout)
AI_DEV_FACTORY_RUNTIME_ROOT=/Users/<you>/runtime/ai-dev-factory
AI_DEV_FACTORY_PROJECT_ROOT=/Users/<you>/runtime/ai-dev-factory/clones/ai-dev-factory

# ── Per-project runtime base root ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Each imported project gets its own isolated runtime rooted at:
#   $RUNTIME_BASE_ROOT/<project_id>/{clones,worktrees,runs,state,logs}/
#
# Defaults to the parent of AI_DEV_FACTORY_RUNTIME_ROOT when not set
# (i.e. ~/runtime for the example path above).
RUNTIME_BASE_ROOT=/Users/<you>/runtime

# ── Docker → host path mapping (read by the supervisor) ──────────────────────
#
# The control API runs inside Docker and emits container-side paths
# (/app, /runtime/…). The supervisor — running on the host — uses these
# pairs to rewrite those paths to host-side equivalents before spawning
# analysis / scripts / deploy workers.
#
# Order of resolution:
#   1. CONTAINER_PROJECT_ROOT → HOST_PROJECT_ROOT  (project root, /app)
#   2. CONTAINER_RUNTIME_ROOT → HOST_RUNTIME_ROOT  (runtime, /runtime)
#   3. identity fallback (path returned unchanged with a log line)
#
# Longest container prefix wins to avoid ambiguous matches such as /app
# accidentally capturing /applications.
CONTAINER_PROJECT_ROOT=/app
HOST_PROJECT_ROOT=/Users/<you>/runtime/ai-dev-factory/clones/ai-dev-factory

CONTAINER_RUNTIME_ROOT=/runtime
HOST_RUNTIME_ROOT=/Users/<you>/runtime/ai-dev-factory

# Managed projects' runtimes live as siblings under RUNTIME_BASE_ROOT (e.g.
# ${RUNTIME_BASE_ROOT}/<project_id>), NOT under HOST_RUNTIME_ROOT. The whole
# base is bind-mounted into the API container at CONTAINER_RUNTIME_BASE so
# filesystem-backed endpoints (tickets list, logs, plan/review/diffs) work for
# every project — not just ai-dev-factory (mounted at CONTAINER_RUNTIME_ROOT).
# Override only if you change the container mount path in docker-compose.yml.
CONTAINER_RUNTIME_BASE=/runtime-base

# ── Global reverse-proxy routes (Traefik file provider) ───────────────────────
#
# Sandbox pretty URLs depend on route files under::
#
#     ${HOST_RUNTIME_ROOT}/proxy/routes/<sandbox_id>.yml
#
# This MUST be the same host directory mounted into the global Traefik
# container (see deploy/infra/docker-compose.traefik.yml → :/routes).
#
# Per-sandbox AI_DEV_FACTORY_RUNTIME_ROOT (…/sandboxes/<id>/runtime) is
# for supervisor state/logs ONLY — proxy routes never go there.
# resolve_proxy_routes_dir() in infra_service_manager.py enforces this.

# ── Sandbox root (host-side, outside the main runtime hierarchy) ──────────────
#
# Sandboxes are created at {SANDBOX_ROOT}/{PROJECT_NAME}/{sandbox_id}/.
# SANDBOX_ROOT must be accessible to both the host (supervisor, workers) and
# the Docker container (via the bind-mount configured in docker-compose.yml).
#
# PROJECT_NAME disambiguates projects that share the same SANDBOX_ROOT.
# Defaults to the basename of AI_DEV_FACTORY_PROJECT_ROOT when not set.
SANDBOX_ROOT=~/sandboxes
PROJECT_NAME=ai-dev-factory

# ── Docker → host sandbox path mapping (read by the supervisor) ───────────────
#
# Mirrors the CONTAINER_RUNTIME_ROOT / HOST_RUNTIME_ROOT pattern.
# The Docker API container sees sandboxes at /sandboxes (the volume mount
# below); the supervisor rewrites those paths to the host equivalent.
CONTAINER_SANDBOX_ROOT=/sandboxes
HOST_SANDBOX_ROOT=~/sandboxes

# ── Supervisor URL & port (shared by both halves) ────────────────────────────
#
# The supervisor binds to 127.0.0.1:<port> on the host. There are TWO
# URLs because the supervisor has two kinds of caller:
#
#   * AI_DEV_FACTORY_SUPERVISOR_URL — used by Docker containers
#     (e.g. the control API). They reach the host via
#     `host.docker.internal:<port>` (works on macOS and on Linux with
#     `host-gateway` configured).
#
#   * AI_DEV_FACTORY_SUPERVISOR_HEALTH_URL — used by host-side shell
#     scripts (start.sh, healthcheck.sh). The `host.docker.internal`
#     hostname is NOT resolvable from a host shell, so we point those
#     scripts at the loopback interface instead. Using SUPERVISOR_URL
#     from a host script previously made every healthcheck fail.
AI_DEV_FACTORY_SUPERVISOR_PORT=8090
AI_DEV_FACTORY_SUPERVISOR_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8090
AI_DEV_FACTORY_SUPERVISOR_HEALTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090

# ── Runtime store backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# "sqlite" (default) stores a file under the runtime root. On macOS that path is
# a Docker bind-mount shared between the container (API) and the host
# (supervisor/daemon); SQLite file locking is unreliable there → corruption.
#
# "postgres" uses the networked db service (docker-compose.yml): a SINGLE
# database (RUNTIME_DB_NAME) holding project-scoped rows (every table has a
# project_id column). Easier to back up/monitor and immune to bind-mount
# corruption. ALL THREE PROCESSES MUST AGREE on the backend, or the board goes
# split-brain:
#   - Docker API container : RUNTIME_DB_HOST is overridden to "db" in compose.
#   - host supervisor/daemon: reach the same server at 127.0.0.1 (below).
# The daemon inherits these from the supervisor (start_supervisor.sh sources
# this file) and is tagged with --project <project_id> so its rows are scoped.
#
# IMPORTANT: Postgres mode NEVER falls back to SQLite. If RUNTIME_DB_BACKEND=postgres
# but psycopg is missing or the server is unreachable, startup FAILS LOUDLY with a
# clear error — it does not silently switch to SQLite. A backend mismatch between
# the API, the supervisor and the daemon is a configuration error (it would create
# an invisible API/Postgres + daemon/SQLite split-brain).
RUNTIME_DB_BACKEND=sqlite
RUNTIME_DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
RUNTIME_DB_PORT=5432
RUNTIME_DB_USER=adf
RUNTIME_DB_PASSWORD=adf
RUNTIME_DB_NAME=adf

# ── GitHub integration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal access token with repo + issues scopes.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# GitHub repository in owner/repo format (e.g. myorg/my-project).
GITHUB_REPO=

# Label used to identify issues ready for AI processing.
# GITHUB_ISSUE_LABEL=ai-ready

# ── Daemon (host-side, V1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The daemon is NOT containerised in V1. Run it on the host with RUNTIME_ROOT
# pointing at the same path used above so it shares state with the API:
#
#   bash deploy/start_supervisor.sh            # in one terminal
#   docker compose up -d                       # in another
#
# Command passed to run_ticket.py --auto for each step.
# DAEMON_EXEC_CMD=claude --dangerously-skip-permissions

# Polling interval in seconds.
# DAEMON_INTERVAL=30

# Maximum concurrent ticket workers.
# DAEMON_MAX_WORKERS=1
